  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+{y}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({y}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)+{y}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)+{y}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x) & =(\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x))+{y}^{5}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\  & =((1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x))+{y}^{5}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+{y}^{5}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x \\\\  & =(1+{y}^{5})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
